#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: a red coat
#> pause: 40
#> must: the red door and the red ring
#> must: a red coat
#> not: scarlet door
#> not: ruby ring
#> source: \|
# 10. One of several words. Pement: gsed 's/scarlet\|ruby\|puce/red/g'
# \| is alternation: the pattern matches any one of the three colours, and g
# recolours every one on the line. It is a GNU extension; the portable form
# on the sheet is three substitutions,  s/scarlet/red/g;s/ruby/red/g;s/puce/red/g
# Try: #ARGS -E  on the line above the program, then write  scarlet|ruby|puce
s/scarlet\|ruby\|puce/red/g

#DATA
the scarlet door and the ruby ring
a puce coat
one more ruby door
